      "file": "items/lem-yangian-gl2-one-root-bethe-cancellation.md",
      "item_id": "lem-yangian-gl2-one-root-bethe-cancellation",
      "status": "repair",
      "strategy": "direct",
      "proposed_proof": "**Given:** The RTT presentation for $N=2$, a representation, and a vector satisfying the displayed vacuum eigenvalue conditions.\n\n[F1] [[lem-yangian-rtt-component-commutator-form]]: $x[t_{ij}(u),t_{kl}(v)]=i(t_{kj}(v)t_{il}(u)-t_{kj}(u)t_{il}(v))$ for $x=u-v$.\n\n\n\n1.1 Apply [F1] to $(i,j,k,l)=(1,2,1,1)$ and interchange $u,v$; rearranging gives $A(u)B(v)=\\frac{x-i}{x}B(v)A(u)+\\frac{i}{x}B(u)A(v)$ for $x=u-v\\ne0$. Applying [F1] to $(i,j,k,l)=(2,2,1,2)$ gives $D(u)B(v)=\\frac{x+i}{x}B(v)D(u)-\\frac{i}{x}B(u)D(v)$. All divisions are by the stated nonzero scalar $x$. [given, F1, algebra]\n\n2.1 Apply these identities to $\\Omega$ and use its eigenvalue conditions. The coefficient of $B(u)\\Omega$ in $(A(u)+D(u))B(v)\\Omega$ is $i(a(v)-d(v))/x$, which vanishes under $a(v)=d(v)$. The remaining coefficient of $B(v)\\Omega$ is exactly $\\Lambda_v(u)$, so the claimed eigenvector identity follows; nonzero-ness of $B(v)\\Omega$ makes it an eigenvector rather than merely a zero-vector identity. [given, step 1.1, algebra] ∎"
    },
    {
      "file": "items/lem-yangian-rtt-spectral-rescaling.md",
      "item_id": "lem-yangian-rtt-spectral-rescaling",
      "status": "repair",
      "strategy": "direct",
      "proposed_proof": "**Given:** $N\\ge2$, $R_i(x)=xI+iP_N$, the RTT relation, and the evaluation-module formula of [[def-yangian-evaluation-module]].\n\n[F1] [[def-yangian-gl-n-rtt-presentation]]: $R_i(x)=xI+iP_N$ and $R_i(u-v)T_1(u)T_2(v)=T_2(v)T_1(u)R_i(u-v)$.\n\n[F2] [[def-yangian-evaluation-module]]: $t_{ij}(u)=\\delta_{ij}I-i\\rho(E_{ij})/(u-a)$.\n\n\n\n1.1 Direct substitution gives $R_i(-i(z-w))=-i((z-w)I-P_N)=-iR_0(z-w)$. [given, F1, algebra]\n\n2.1 Substitute $u=-iz$ and $v=-iw$ in the RTT relation [F1]. By step 1.1, each side has the same nonzero scalar factor $-i$, which cancels; the resulting relation is $R_0(z-w)\\widetilde T_1(z)\\widetilde T_2(w)=\\widetilde T_2(w)\\widetilde T_1(z)R_0(z-w)$. [given, F1, step 1.1, algebra]\n\n3.1 In the evaluation module, substitute $u=-iz$ into [F2]. Since $-iz-a=-i(z-ia)$, one obtains $t_{ij}(-iz)=\\delta_{ij}I+\\rho(E_{ij})/(z-ia)$. Thus the shifted standard evaluation parameter is exactly $ia$. [given, F2, algebra] ∎"
    },
